133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 422 0 R
/E (The Digital Library & Paperless Learning Resource Management System is a C++-based application designed to manage and access educational resources digitally. It provides a centralized platform for storing, organizing, searching, and retrieving resources such as e-books, notes, question papers, study materials, and research papers. The main objective is to reduce the use of physical documents and promote a paperless learning environment. Students can easily search and access required learning materials, while administrators can add, update, delete, and manage resources efficiently. The system uses Object-Oriented Programming concepts in C++, including classes, objects, encapsulation, inheritance, polymorphism, and file handling. It improves the accessibility, efficiency, and organization of academic resources while reducing paperwork and manual record maintenance.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
